        "settings.rules.prompt.copy": "Copy prompt",
        "settings.rules.prompt.copied": "Copied",
        "settings.rules.prompt.import": "Import rule from clipboard",
        "settings.rules.prompt.error.noJSON": "No JSON on the clipboard — copy the model's full reply.",
        "settings.rules.prompt.error.badJSON": "That JSON didn't parse; it may be truncated. Ask the model for a single JSON object and retry.",
        "settings.rules.prompt.error.samePrompt": "That's still the prompt itself — send it to a model first, then copy the reply.",
        "settings.rules.prompt.template": "You are a rule generator for Clipth, a macOS clipboard manager. Generate one rule for the request below and output only a single JSON object — no commentary, no Markdown code fence.\n\n# My request\n{{REQUEST}}\n\n# Rule model\nA rule = when it runs + match conditions + one action. Fields:\n- name: string, required, the rule's display name\n- triggers: array of \"copy\" and/or \"paste\", default [\"copy\"]. copy = runs as a clip is captured and changes what gets stored; paste = runs as text leaves Clipth for another app and changes only that paste, leaving history untouched\n- apps: array of bundle ids (e.g. \"com.apple.Safari\") scoping the rule to a source app (copy) or a target app (paste); omit for every app\n- categories: array of \"text\"/\"image\"/\"video\"/\"audio\"/\"file\"; omit for every kind. text covers plain text, links and rich text; audio is recognised by file extension\n- contentMatch: {\"mode\":\"any\"|\"contains\"|\"notContains\"|\"regex\",\"value\":\"…\"} applied to textual clips\n- fileNameMatch: same shape, applied to a file clip's name\n- fileExtensions: array like [\"mp3\",\"m4a\"], no dots; omit for any extension\n- action: required, one of:\n  - {\"type\":\"drop\"} — matching clips never enter history\n  - {\"type\":\"replaceRegex\",\"pattern\":\"…\",\"replacement\":\"…\"} — regex replace, $1 refers to a group\n  - {\"type\":\"javascript\",\"source\":\"…\"}\n  - {\"type\":\"shell\",\"source\":\"…\"}\n- timeoutSeconds: number, script timeout in seconds, 0–30, default 3\n\n# Script environment (important)\nJavaScript runs in a JavaScriptCore sandbox with **no** network, filesystem, require, fetch, atob/btoa, setTimeout, DOM or Node APIs. You get standard JS syntax, JSON, regular expressions, and these injected globals:\n  clip = { text, type, sourceApp, bundleId, tags }\n  console.log(...) — shown in the rule editor's test panel\nWrite `function run(clip) { … }`; the return value decides the effect:\n  a string → replace the clip's text\n  { text, tags, title, newClip, copy, drop } → richer effects (tags appends tags, title renames, newClip stores a separate clip, copy writes to the pasteboard, drop:true discards)\n  null → skip, change nothing\nNote: on the paste trigger only text replacement applies; tags/title/drop are ignored.\n\nShell scripts live inline in `source` and run from a temp file; a leading #!/bin/sh or #!/usr/bin/env python3 picks the interpreter. The clip arrives on stdin; metadata comes in CLIP_TYPE / CLIP_SOURCE_APP / CLIP_BUNDLE_ID / CLIP_TAGS / CLIP_IMAGE_PATH. stdout is the result: plain text replaces the clip, a JSON envelope (same keys as above) gives richer effects, empty means no-op; a non-zero exit means skip; stderr shows up in the test panel. Avoid network calls and anything destructive.\n\n# Example\n{\"name\":\"Strip tracking params\",\"triggers\":[\"copy\"],\"categories\":[\"text\"],\"contentMatch\":{\"mode\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"utm_\"},\"action\":{\"type\":\"javascript\",\"source\":\"function run(clip) {\\n  var out = clip.text.replace(/([?&])(utm_[^=]+|fbclid|gclid)=[^&#]*/g, '$1').replace(/[?&]+(#|$)/g, '$1');\\n  return out === clip.text ? null : out;\\n}\"}}\n\n# Output rules\n- Emit that one JSON object and nothing else, unfenced\n- Escape newlines inside `source` as \\n so the JSON stays valid\n- Prefer replaceRegex over a script when it can do the job; keep scripts short and side-effect free\n- Keep the match conditions tight so the rule doesn't fire on everything",
